C o m p i l a t i o n


      CEE 6410 - Water Resources Systems Analysis
      HW3 - Problem 1
       
      THE PROBLEM:
       
      A reservoir operator wants a release schedule that will maximize profit.  Data are as fol-lows:
       
       
       
                      Determine the optimal volume of water to divert each month.
       
      THE SOLUTION:
      Uses General Algebraic Modeling System to Solve this Linear Program
       
      Isabel I. Hinton
      isabel.hinton@usu.edu
      September 28, 2026
  20   
  21  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  22  SETS time time at the end of the month /June, July, August/
  23       place place the water is being stored /reservoir, spill, diversion/;
  24   
  25  Alias (time,tprev);
  26   
  27  * 2. DEFINE input data
  28  PARAMETERS
  29     Table c(time, place) Objective function constants
  30              reservoir   spill   diversion
  31     June         0         0       150
  32     July         0         0       170
  33     August       0         0       425;
  34   
  35   
  36     Parameters
  37     b(time) Right hand constraint values (per month)
  38      /June    9000,
  39       July    9000,
  40      August   9000/
  41   
  42      i(time) Inflow constraints (per month)
  43      /June    5000,
  44      July     3200,
  45      August   2000/;
  46   
  47    TABLE A(time,place) Left hand side constraint coefficients
  48              reservoir     spill     diversion
  49      June     1              0          0
  50      July     1              0          0
  51      August   1              0          0;
  52   
  53   
  54  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  55  VARIABLES X(time,place) Water released by the end of the month to each place
  56            VPROFIT  total profit ($);
  57   
  58  * Non-negativity constraints
  59  POSITIVE VARIABLES X;
  60   
  61  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  62  EQUATIONS
  63     PROFIT Total profit ($) and objective function value
  64     MAX_STORAGE(time) Resource Constraints
  65     MIN_STORAGE minimum storage constraint for august
  66     MASS_BALANCE(time);
  67   
  68  PROFIT..                 VPROFIT =E= SUM((time,place), c(time,place)*X(time,place));
  69  MAX_STORAGE(time) ..    SUM(place, A(time,place)*X(time, "reservoir")) =L= b(time);
  70  MIN_STORAGE..           X("August", "reservoir") =G= 3000;
  71  MASS_BAlANCE(time)..         X(time, "reservoir")
  72                             - sum(tprev$(ord(tprev) = ord(time)-1), X(tprev,"reservoir")) - 3000$(ord(time)=1)
  73                             + X(time, "spill")
  74                             + X(time, "diversion")
  75                             =E= i(time);
  76   
  77   
  78  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  79  MODEL RELEASE /PROFIT, MAX_STORAGE, MIN_STORAGE, MASS_BALANCE/;
  80  *Altnerative way to write (include all previously defined equations)
  81  *MODEL PLANTING /ALL/;
  82   
  83   
  84  * 6. SOLVE the MODEL
  85  * Solve the PLANTING model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  86  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  87  SOLVE RELEASE USING LP MAXIMIZING VPROFIT;
  88   
  89   
  90  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file


